---js
{
  layout: "layouts/base.webc",
  meta: {
    title: "The DynamoDB conformance suite",
    description: "How faithfully does each DynamoDB emulator match the real thing? An independent conformance suite, scored against live AWS DynamoDB and tracked run over run.",
  },
  // The home page renders the latest run's standings, so its freshness tracks
  // the data, not this file's git date. Keeps the sitemap <lastmod> honest.
  eleventyComputed: {
    lastmod: (data) => data.conformance?.latest?.date,
  },
}
---

<standings-table></standings-table>

<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pb-20">
  <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
    <a href="/about" class="group rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-white/10 p-5 hover:border-brand-300 dark:hover:border-brand-500/40 transition-colors">
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1 group-hover:text-brand-700 dark:group-hover:text-brand-300">Why this exists →</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">What the conformance suite measures, and why "works with the AWS SDK" isn't the same as matching DynamoDB.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/runs" class="group rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-white/10 p-5 hover:border-brand-300 dark:hover:border-brand-500/40 transition-colors">
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1 group-hover:text-brand-700 dark:group-hover:text-brand-300">Browse past runs →</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">Step back through every recorded run to see how each emulator's conformance has shifted over time.</p>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
